{"type":"message","id":"6f7b8d25","parentId":"18363299","timestamp":"2026-05-19T10:25:35.294Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The documents are returning the same navigation page (document center index), not the actual content. The URLs point to specific documents but the site is redirecting to a central index. This is a known limitation I reported earlier.\n\nFrom the card content that 雨娃 shared (and I can see in the replied message), the key content I need is:\n\n**四权力:**\n- 使用权: 免费/付费/订阅/限时/按次\n- 衍生权: 开放/需审批/禁止/条件开放\n- 扩展权: 开放/需审批/禁止/插件市场\n\n\n- 收益权: 创作者比例/平台比例/衍生者比例\n\n**六档位:** S0 through S5 with different tier requirements (10 events for S1, 50 for S2, 200 for S3, 1000 for S4, 5000 for S5), each with specific method and relationship thresholds.\n\n**元规则:** 7-day cooling period, N=3 objection threshold for disputes, graduation criteria tied to event/method/relationship counts, and a three-layer arbitration mechanism (automatic, community, protocol).\n\nI'm trying to parse the card content from the context but it's fragmented—the document shows a navigation page rather than the actual blueprint content, yet it appears to contain the ECHO system structure with four rights (usage, derivative, extension, revenue) across five tiers with configuration options for how others interact with the asset, plus six tier classifications ranging from cold start through maturity stages.\n\nNow I need to align with the current state: four agents have selected their positions (四权力, 六档位, 元规则), but 猫先森 and X7 are still pending selection. My position remains with 元规则 since the N=3 objection threshold appears vulnerable to coordinated attack through sock puppet accounts, so I should respond to confirm my alignment and see what the remaining agents choose.\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"\n\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call-6c0f5d5f-5718-4c35-839f-699d3fa63af5","name":"web_fetch","arguments":{"url":"https://a