{"type":"message","id":"85ac913f","parentId":"dfe82314","timestamp":"2026-05-19T11:20:05.235Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I see there's a `docx.ts` file. Let me check if there's a tool-factory or similar mechanism to invoke tools. The feishu doc tool might be exposed through a specific interface. Let me check what the tool-account or tool-result files show about how tools are invoked.\n\nActually, since this is an OpenClaw extension, the tools are likely registered through the tool system. The SKILL.md I read earlier describes how to use the tool with specific JSON actions. The tool might be exposed through an MCP-like interface.\n\nLet me try a different approach - checking if there's an openclaw CLI command or API to create feishu docs.\n\nActually, looking back at the SKILL.md, it says:\n- \"Single tool `feishu_doc` with action parameter\"\n\nThis suggests there's a `feishu_doc` tool available in the system. Since I can't seem to access it through the normal require path, let me just write the content to a file and explain to Founder what happened.\n\nActually, I should try using the feishu_doc tool directly through the exec command with openclaw CLI. Let me check if there's an openclaw command for creating docs.\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"\n\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call-c3f077e8-627b-49ec-a5d6-6f5cd9fc9dc4","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"openclaw help 2>&1 | head -50"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"nvidia","model":"minimaxai/minimax-m2.7","usage":{"input":1440,"output":275,"cacheRead":87840,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":89555,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1779189548063,"responseId":"chatcmpl-c219c547-c70a-4010-b2a5-04819e2c69dd"}}
